`collectTasks` reads files **sequentially** in a loop. With 100+ markdown files, this is 100 serial `vault.read()` calls.

```js
// BAD: serial
for (const file of files) {
  const text = await this.readMarkdownFileContent(file);
  results.push(...this.scanTasksInContent(file, text));
}

// FIX: parallel
const entries = await Promise.all(
  files.map(async file => {
    const text = await this.readMarkdownFileContent(file);
    return this.scanTasksInContent(file, text);
  })
);
return this.sortTasksForKanban(entries.flat());
```

---

`STATUSES.indexOf(a.status)` is O(n) and called **O(k log k)** times per sort (k = task count). Also `getTaskTouchedKey()` recomputed per comparison pair.

```js
// BAD: O(STATUSES.length) per comparison
const statusDiff = STATUSES.indexOf(a.status) - STATUSES.indexOf(b.status);

// FIX: precompute before sort
const statusIndex = new Map(STATUSES.map((s, i) => [s, i]));
const touchedMap = new Map(items.map(t => [t, this.getTaskTouchedKey(t)]));
return items.sort((a, b) => {
  // ...use statusIndex.get(a.status) and touchedMap.get(a)
});
```

---

Filter by `status.key` runs **twice** — once to set innerHTML, once to count for headers.

```js
// BAD: two passes
items.map(task => this.formatKanbanCellItem(task)).join("")
// ...later...
const count = visibleTasks.filter(task => task.status.key === status.key).length;

// FIX: group once
const byStatus = new Map(STATUSES.map(s => [s.key, []]));
for (const task of visibleTasks) byStatus.get(task.status.key)?.push(task);
// then use byStatus.get(status.key) in both places
```

---

`getComputedStyle(text).lineHeight` forces style recalc for **every card** on every refresh. All cards share the same line-height.

```js
// BAD: per-card style recalc
const lineHeight = Number.parseFloat(getComputedStyle(text).lineHeight) || 18;

// FIX: compute once outside loop
const cards = element.querySelectorAll(".task-kanban-inline-card");
const firstText = cards[0]?.querySelector(".task-kanban-inline-text");
const lineHeight = firstText
  ? (Number.parseFloat(getComputedStyle(firstText).lineHeight) || 18)
  : 18;
for (const card of cards) { /* use lineHeight */ }
```

---

```js
// BAD: expensive & fragile (key order)
const headingObjects = Array.from(
  new Set(tasks.map(t => JSON.stringify(t.heading || "")).map(s => JSON.parse(s)))
);

// FIX: deduplicate by text directly
const seen = new Set();
const headingObjects = [];
for (const task of tasks) {
  const text = task.heading?.text || (typeof task.heading === "string" ? task.heading : "");
  if (!seen.has(text)) { seen.add(text); headingObjects.push(task.heading || ""); }
}
```

---

Sorts `headings` by `localeCompare`, then builds a `Map` (which is insertion-ordered but into a deduplicated map, so sort result is irrelevant since it iterates the Map). The `.sort()` call is wasted CPU.

```js
// current: sorts, then deduplicates losing the sort
const headings = headingObjects.filter(Boolean).map(...).sort(...);
const uniqueHeadings = new Map(); // insertion order = sort order? Only if no dupes
```

If sort is intentional, sort **after** deduplication:
```js
const unique = [...new Map(headings.map(h => [h.text, h])).values()];
unique.sort((a, b) => a.text.localeCompare(b.text));
```

